# Lost Chick, WindurstWoods's owners one by one (the coverage of every owner's trigger and update). A level 30 Warrior,
# ENABLE_CHOCOBO_RAISING on. Each owner in turn is the chick's owner (3 clues, location 3: the var is owner + 0x30 +
# 192) and is asked: the owners with an ask option play their own default event, the ask, then the guess (right:
# updateEvent(1, 1, 1), the Story of a Diligent Chocobo); the owners without one play their question event on trigger
# (priorityEvent, 1) and the guess is the update. Then the same with the next owner as the chick's owner (wrong:
# updateEvent(0, 0, 0), WRONG_OWNER). The trace shows the default event of each ask owner.
lists WindurstWoods/onEventUpdate/340 WindurstWoods/onEventUpdate/277 WindurstWoods/onEventUpdate/424 WindurstWoods/onEventUpdate/420 WindurstWoods/onEventUpdate/483 WindurstWoods/onEventUpdate/486
char zone=WindurstWoods pos=130,-5,-117 job=WAR lvl=30
login
charvar [ChocoboRaising]LostChick 242   # owner 2, right at Kapeh_Myohrye
trigger Kapeh_Myohrye
update 340 option=1
update 340 option=2
finish
charvar [ChocoboRaising]LostChick 244   # owner 4, right at Kororo
trigger Kororo
update 277 option=2
update 277 option=3
finish
charvar [ChocoboRaising]LostChick 245   # owner 5, right at Gioh_Ajihri
trigger Gioh_Ajihri
update 424 option=1
update 424 option=2
finish
charvar [ChocoboRaising]LostChick 246   # owner 6, right at Gottah_Maporushanoh
trigger Gottah_Maporushanoh
update 420 option=1
update 420 option=2
update 483 option=1
update 483 option=2
update 486 option=1
update 486 option=2
finish
